    "result_text": "The implementation is complete. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the suite (the other files in the `acceptance` package are support classes), and the full build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required: *On successful create, enqueue a welcome notification \u2014 emit via the logger named `NOTIFY` a line containing the owner id and the memberId.*\n\nI made two changes in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger alongside the existing `AUDIT` one:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n   ```\n\n2. Emitted the welcome line in `addOwner(...)` right after the owner is persisted and the audit events fire (so it only runs on a successful create, after all validation/quota/conflict checks have passed):\n   ```java\n   NOTIFY.info(\"welcome notification: owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   ```\n\nThis follows the existing pattern in the controller (the `AUDIT` logger uses the same SLF4J parameterized style). The line carries both `owner.getId()` and `owner.getMemberId()` \u2014 the same `memberId` value the DTO exposes \u2014 satisfying `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome`, which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a message contains both the id and the memberId.\n\n`BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
